ws and retained full candidate records."},{"id":"cdmo-business-correction-fresh-pair","text":"A changed batch, product, destination, disposition or approval basis requires a new dossier and both fresh independent human decisions over the exact corrected noncircular context."},{"id":"cdmo-canonical-human-subjects","text":"The host selects canonical human-subject identities across parties and resolves account aliases before exact actor-separation checks; authentication of physical-person distinctness remains external."},{"id":"cdmo-changed-evidence-fresh-decisions","text":"An invalidating required-evidence, agreement, destination or transfer-result change makes old decisions unusable; the changed dossier needs both fresh independent decisions."},{"id":"cdmo-closed-native-request","text":"One quantity-free native operation contains exactly the 14 selected source fields; no hidden shipment, invented quantity, approval-evidence body or caller-selected quality revision is added."},{"id":"cdmo-complete-attributable-completion","text":"Completion is the exact full attributable generated event with all request bindings, operation identity, event identity/time, previous/resulting inventory revisions and committed quality revision."},{"id":"cdmo-complete-current-hold-absence","text":"Current complete authoritative absence covers blocking holds at batch, product and site scope; stale, incomplete, unavailable or contradictory responses never establish absence."},{"id":"cdmo-complete-prior-attempt-history","text":"A complete current batch/site/candidate-keyed history assertion excludes the registered candidate and blocks every other unresolved or possibly in-flight attempt; all other attempt/status/effect writers join the guarded scoped revision."},{"id":"cdmo-correction-no-effect-or-release","text":"Correction evidence neither establishes the old effect, overwrites an event, releases claims, revives a permit nor opens a new execution opportunity."},{"id":"cdmo-current-executor-boundary","text":"The exact executor has current session, occupancy, credentials and execution authority at proposal and dispatch; a different actor requires a new proposal."},{"id":"cdmo-decision-authority-scope-guards","text":"Each guarded party authority-scope record binds the complete selected root/envelope/capacity reliance-subject digest and absence of applicable revocation; every selected revocation/remit writer joins commitment coordination."},{"id":"cdmo-decision-effective-intervals","text":"Both decisions use inclusive 2026-10-06T12:00:00Z and exclusive 2026-10-07T12:00:00Z bounds, with independently attributable earlier withdrawal or invalidation."},{"id":"cdmo-deviation-investigation-and-disposition","text":"Every deviation has attributable authorized human quality disposition, investigation and required follow-up; OPEN, UNINVESTIGATED, unresolved failures and missing evidence block without model waiver."},{"id":"cdmo-dual-native-new-status-binding","text":"The single real new_status field must independently satisfy request equality and completion-success membership; old_status remains separately bound and no outcome-status field is invented."},{"id":"cdmo-durable-attempt-history-and-claims","text":"Retain authoritative transaction/history state before connector invocation and retain occupied request/disposition claims after a possibly sent or uncertain request across restart, abandonment and expiry."},{"id":"cdmo-exact-decision-endpoints","text":"Each human decision context includes exact inclusive/exclusive INSTANT endpoints equal to its complete envelope; provider intervals cannot widen authority and current-reliance cutoffs can shorten dispatch authorization."},{"id":"cdmo-exact-linked-correction","text":"The correction binds original event identity/digest, expected revision, every exact old/new value, complete corrected inventory, authorizing decision, actor and separate event time; history is append-only."},{"id":"cdmo-exact-prerequisite-record-revisions","text":"Every prerequisite binds the selected exact subject, source record revision and content; a passing different batch, specification or superseded record fails."},{"id":"cdmo-exact-request-and-transition","text":"Bind the exact request, batch, site, product revision, customer, old/new status and expected inventory revision; create no shipment order or quantity/location/possession change."},{"id":"cdmo-fictional-policy-and-review","text":"The source, people, provider capabilities and selected organizational rules are fictional and provisional; neither Genezen procedures nor regulatory applicability or endorsement is established."},{"id":"cdmo-fresh-correction-issue-identities","text":"Business corrections need both new immutable human issue ids, new act ids/digests and changed dossier revision/digest relative to original request/native/retained decisions; revision-only renewal is insufficient."},{"id":"cdmo-high-materiality-existing-gate","text":"The HIGH materiality/LOW reversibility DECIDE execution gate selects the independently admitted Cedar human decision with exactly translated status criteria, without a third approval."},{"id":"cdmo-historical-authorization-revision-binding","text":"The committed quality revision equals the selected coordinator observation revision in the exact authorization used by this dispatch, including late effects and restart; newer reads or other authorizations cannot replace it."},{"id":"cdmo-historical-signer-reliance","text":"Historical signer departure is usable only under explicit selected root/capacity/channel survival terms and current applicable remit/revocation evidence within the decision interval."},{"id":"cdmo-human-signing-authority","text":"Each independent positive human decision has complete authentic signing-time role, occupancy and party-specific remit evidence; machines supply neither decision."},{"id":"cdmo-immutable-historical-commit-revision","text":"This correction profile forbids authorization-bound commit-revision changes and cannot supply missing/invalid historical commit data; a separate provider procedure remains outside the class."},{"id":"cdmo-immutable-predecision-dossier","text":"The complete immutable dossier binds exact manufacturing-evidence identities/revisions/digests and excludes both decision records and their digests."},{"id":"cdmo-independent-correction-authority","text":"A correction requires the current Custodian role, attributable return and exact current Head of Quality authorization, separate from fresh business decisions."},{"id":"cdmo-laboratory-release-conclusions","text":"The exact authenticated batch/specification release panel supplies attributable PASS conclusions for identity, vector-genome titer, product-specific potency, endotoxin and microbiological safety under approved methods."},{"id":"cdmo-late-historical-effect-and-conflict","text":"Late exact evidence may establish the historical effect and consume its claims without reopening; changed or additional native facts remain retained conflicts requiring investigation."},{"id":"cdmo-later-instance-fresh-basis-and-history","text":"Later work needs a new request/dossier, both fresh decisions, conclusively established old history and current inventory prerequisites/duplicate checks; unknown effect or inventory still APPROVED blocks repeating the old transition."},{"id":"cdmo-manufacturing-completeness","text":"The exact manufacturing record establishes every required operation and review as complete."},{"id":"cdmo-named-record-owners","text":"Manufacturing, laboratory, investigation, quality, inventory custody and procedure/remit owners retain their named separate duties; custody not supplied by the source remains explicit."},{"id":"cdmo-noncircular-decision-context","text":"Both decisions bind the exhaustive shared business context and may bind their own identity; neither binds the other decision identity/digest, finished execution digest or future event."},{"id":"cdmo-postcommit-hold-containment","text":"A later hold preserves the original event and creates a separate named-owner protected containment alert duty; promptly supplies no numerical deadline and this specimen does not prove detection or delivery."},{"id":"cdmo-postdispatch-executor-boundary","text":"A session end or ordinary occupancy expiry after valid dispatch alone does not cancel the in-flight attempt; covered remit revocations and quality changes still block before commit."},{"id":"cdmo-proposal-and-dispatch-live-queries","text":"Every selected mutable prerequisite is queried for the exact proposal and dispatch instant with authentic revision and applicability; cached substitutes fail."},{"id":"cdmo-protected-audit-evidence","text":"Complete signer/source authority details belong to protected internal audit interfaces; ordinary connector callers receive only the declared closed safe status/digest carriers."},{"id":"cdmo-quality-agreement-allocation","text":"Use the exact applicable Cedar/Alder quality agreement and its responsibility allocation; Cedar owns manufacturing-output disposition and Alder retains final drug-product release."},{"id":"cdmo-quality-agreement-changes","text":"Signed supersession or withdrawal invalidates affected pending authorization; a revision cannot retrospectively change retained events or silently move approval to a new responsibility allocation."},{"id":"cdmo-quality-coordinator-coverage","text":"The authoritative quality revision covers all selected evidence, decisions, remits, agreement and holds and every relevant writer participates in affected-authorization invalidation."},{"id":"cdmo-referral-intent-only","text":"Failed quality checks retain the Quality Review Queue intent; inventory uncertainty also names the Custodian; intent alone supplies neither delivery, resolution nor authority."},{"id":"cdmo-regulatory-industry-integration-review","text":"Regulatory, industry and integration review must confirm applicability, responsibilities, evidence inventory, terminology and real provider guarantees; no committed reviewer or company endorsement is inferred."},{"id":"cdmo-request-identity-uniqueness","text":"The complete source request identity is unique across every writer and cannot be bypassed with fresh business approval or a changed dossier."},{"id":"cdmo-scope-administrative-only","text":"Authorize only the declared administrative inventory status update; manufacturing, movement, shipment, patient administration and final drug-product release remain outside this work class."},{"id":"cdmo-source-owner-amendment-procedures","text":"Named owners alone amend laboratory, manufacturing, agreement and regulatory source records through separate procedures; the inventory agent cannot do so."},{"id":"cdmo-source-successor-and-claim-limits","text":"Source changes require explicit successor identity and reassessment; this draft establishes no source acceptance, implementation, conformance, provider validation or publication."},{"id":"cdmo-two-independent-business-decisions","text":"Both complete attributable human decisions independently approve the same predecision dossier and exact business context; neither supplies the other party’s authority."},{"id":"cdmo-uncertain-completion-stop-retain","text":"No event, missing/mismatched completion, stale/incomplete/unavailable/ambiguous history or conflicting evidence stops and retains the request, evidence and claims; no blind resend, rollback or automatic successor follows."}],"revision":"revision-3-CV-TRANSFER-042","schema":"seampoint.work-class/1.0.0-draft.3/authority-source"},"specification_pin":"sha256:fd52d69dd3c3546bff2cec9d46fb8d6b942fd57b77b0a3ab8377a592e80d00b6","work_class":{"authority_profile":"EVIDENCE_ONLY","id":"cdmo-cedar-human-decision","revision":"3","schema":"seampoint.work-class/1.0.0-draft.3/authority-work-class","steps":[{"exclusive_keys":[],"executor_role":"quality-disposition-reviewer","fields":[{"name":"agreement_id","type_ref":"IDENTITY"},{"name":"agreement_revision","type_ref":"REVISION"},{"name":"batch_id","type_ref":"IDENTITY"},{"name":"customer_id","type_ref":"IDENTITY"},{"name":"decision_identity","type_ref":"IDENTITY"},{"name":"decision_revision","type_ref":"REVISION"},{"name":"dossier_digest","type_ref":"IDENTITY"},{"name":"dossier_id","type_ref":"IDENTITY"},{"name":"dossier_revision","type_ref":"REVISION"},{"name":"effective_from","type_ref":"INSTANT"},{"name":"effective_until","type_ref":"INSTANT"},{"name":"executor_role","type_ref":"IDENTITY"},{"name":"expected_inventory_revision","type_ref":"REVISION"},{"name":"new_status","type_ref":"STATUS"},{"name":"old_status","type_ref":"STATUS"},{"name":"product_id","type_ref":"IDENTITY"},{"name":"product_revision","type_ref":"REVISION"},{"name":"request_id","type_ref":"IDENTITY"},{"name":"site_id","type_ref":"IDENTITY"}],"id":"decide-cedar-disposition","interface":"human-quality-decisions","operation":"decide-cedar-disposition","quantity_mode":"NONE","required_credentials":[],"scope_fields":{"resources":["batch_id","site_id"],"subjects":["customer_id"]}}],"types":[{"id":"BOOLEAN","kind":"BOOLEAN","nonnegative":false,"unit":null},{"id":"IDENTITY","kind":"IDENTITY","nonnegative":false,"unit":null},{"id":"INSTANT","kind":"INSTANT","nonnegative":false,"unit":null},{"id":"REVISION","kind":"STRING","nonnegative":false,"unit":null},{"id":"STATUS","kind":"STRING","nonnegative":false,"unit":null}]}},"decision_act_digest":"sha256:f367ba5141afbf4d407278305e73deec104186431cbc0be37e2275bb0f1b271f","schema":"seampoint.work-class/1.0.0-draft.3/human-decision-evidence"}
